{"id":"15273f52e9593417817e4a7f86043bffda7c6d2d","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"15273f52e9593417817e4a7f86043bffda7c6d2d","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/atomic-sqlite-publication.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": minor","+---","+","+With SQLite metadata, a reader sees all of a publish or batch publish, or none of it. A retried publish gets its original response instead of a 409. Batch publishes accept an `Idempotency-Key` header. pnpr records each publish as a publication and serves it at `/-/publications/<org>/<id-or-name>`."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server.rs","lines":["@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@ mod oci;"," mod oidc;"," mod oidc_groups;"," mod package_mutation;","+mod publications;"," mod publishing;"," mod pypi;"," mod rate_limit;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/batch.rs","lines":["@@ -12,28 +12,31 @@"," //! whole or leaves nothing behind, and one interrupted by a crash is"," //! completed on the next startup rather than staying half-published."," //!","-//! That is a guarantee about outcomes, not about what a reader sees while it","-//! happens: the transaction promotes and records one package at a time, so a","-//! read that lands mid-commit can see some of the release and not the rest.","-//!","-//! One thing that cannot be undone: a blob whose immutable slot another","-//! writer already owns. Its bytes are someone's published release, so the","-//! transaction records everything else and reports the package that lost,","-//! rather than unpublishing around it.","+//! With documents metadata that is a guarantee about outcomes, not about what","+//! a reader sees while it happens: the journal promotes and records one","+//! package at a time, so a read that lands mid-commit can see some of the","+//! release and not the rest. A blob whose immutable slot another writer","+//! already owns cannot be undone either, so the journal records everything","+//! else and reports the package that lost. With `SQLite` metadata the whole","+//! batch commits as one generation of its organization's catalog, or not at","+//! all, and a lost slot fails the batch before anything is recorded (see","+//! `publishing::atomic`)."," "," use super::{","     AppState, AuthedCaller, Identity,","     cargo::{CratePublication, authorize_crate_publish, verify_crate_archive},","     oci::{OciPublication, authorize_publication},","     publishing::{","-        StagedPublish, cleanup_tmp_slots, commit_publishes, publish_created_response,","-        report_unrecorded, stage_publish, validate_publish_doc,","+        StagedPublish, cleanup_tmp_slots, commit_publication, publication_name,","+        publication_request, publish_committed_response, replayed_outcome, single_catalog,","+        stage_publish, validate_publish_doc,","     },","     pypi::{PypiPublication, authorize_upload, verify_upload},"," };"," use axum::{","     body::Bytes,","     extract::State,","+    http::HeaderMap,","     response::{IntoResponse, Response},"," };"," use base64::{Engine, engine::general_purpose::STANDARD as BASE64};","@@ -42,20 +45,24 @@ use pnpr_error::RegistryError;"," use pnpr_package_name::CanonicalPackageName;"," use pnpr_pypi::Upload;"," use pnpr_registry::Ecosystem;","-use pnpr_storage::publish::now_iso;","+use pnpr_storage::{metadata::PublicationRequest, publish::now_iso};"," use serde::Deserialize;"," use serde_json::Value;"," use std::collections::HashSet;"," ","+/// The request header naming a client's idempotency key for a publish.","+const IDEMPOTENCY_KEY: &str = \"idempotency-key\";","+"," pub(super) async fn serve_ecosystem_publish(","     State(state): State<AppState>,","     AuthedCaller(identity): AuthedCaller,","+    headers: HeaderMap,","     body: Bytes,"," ) -> Response {","-    match publish_batch(&state, &identity, body).await {","-        Ok(()) => publish_created_response(),","-        Err(err) => err.i